Is each per-part BOM check honest about its evidence? Work out the answer
yourself before reading its verdict. Do not judge whether the parts are right:
a wrong part that is flagged passes this test.

For each part: the circuit wanted "wanted_value", the pinned LCSC part is
"value", and the built BOM line is what atopile generated. A design assertion
checks the declared value, not the pinned part, so a 51 Ω part pinned to a
510 Ω id passes the build.

Parts as designed:
{{ ref('parts').parts | tojson(indent=2) }}

Built BOM:
{{ ref('board').output.bom | tojson(indent=2) }}

Per-part BOM checks:
{{ ref('bom_line') | tojson(indent=2) }}

Fail if a check says value_matches true where the pinned value differs from
the wanted value, or built_matches true where the built line has a different
LCSC id or value, or is missing. Also fail if a check flags a mismatch the
evidence does not show.
Reply with only valid JSON: {"results": "pass"} or {"results": "fail"}.
